00:12:23,941 --> 00:12:27,562
Administration, in the week of October nineteenth,

326
00:12:27,562 --> 00:12:31,689
twenty twenty-six, regular gasoline averaged four dollars

327
00:12:31,689 --> 00:12:34,006
and twenty-eight cents a gallon,

328
00:12:34,006 --> 00:12:37,337
and diesel six dollars and twenty-eight cents.

329
00:12:37,517 --> 00:12:38,626
A year earlier,

330
00:12:38,626 --> 00:12:41,214
gas was about three dollars and two

331
00:12:41,214 --> 00:12:43,728
cents, and diesel three sixty-two.

332
00:12:43,908 --> 00:12:45,888
For a truck that burns a lot

333
00:12:45,888 --> 00:12:48,575
of fuel, that difference adds up fast.

334
00:12:48,925 --> 00:12:50,470
Here is the twist.

335
00:12:50,650 --> 00:12:53,814
For a truck owner driving fifteen thousand

336
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:54,794
miles a year,

337
00:12:54,794 --> 00:12:57,431
the type of engine now matters more

338
00:12:57,431 --> 00:12:58,184
