345
00:13:11,995 --> 00:13:14,325
We cover this in detail in our

346
00:13:14,325 --> 00:13:17,277
diesel versus gas versus hybrid video.

347
00:13:17,627 --> 00:13:19,555
How do you cut fuel costs?

348
00:13:19,735 --> 00:13:22,261
Choose the smallest truck and engine that

349
00:13:22,261 --> 00:13:23,554
really does your job.

350
00:13:23,734 --> 00:13:25,975
Keep tires properly inflated.

351
00:13:26,155 --> 00:13:28,146
Remove heavy items you do not need

352
00:13:28,146 --> 00:13:28,907
from the bed.

353
00:13:29,087 --> 00:13:31,060
Avoid long idling.

354
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:33,814
And remember that lift kits and big

355
00:13:33,814 --> 00:13:36,976
off-road tires usually reduce fuel economy.

356
00:13:37,156 --> 00:13:40,640
Every choice adds up over fifteen thousand

357
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:41,138
miles.

358
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:43,992
There is one more cost that hides

359
00:13:43,992 --> 00:13:45,131
in plain sight:

360
00:13:45,131 --> 00:13:47,559
license, registration and taxes.

361
00:13:47,739 --> 00:13:48,947
According to AAA,

362
00:13:48,947 --> 00:13:51,930
these averaged eight hundred two dollars a

363
00:13:51,930 --> 00:13:53,777
year in twenty twenty-six.

364
00:13:53,957 --> 00:13:55,633
On an expensive truck,

365
00:13:55,633 --> 00:13:58,604
sales tax at purchase can add thousands

366
00:13:58,604 --> 00:14:02,108
more, and some states charge registration fees

367
00:14:02,108 --> 00:14:05,079
based on the vehicle's value or weight.

368
00:14:05,428 --> 00:14:08,275
And then there are costs AAA does

369
00:14:08,275 --> 00:14:09,742
not count at all:

370
00:14:09,742 --> 00:14:12,158
parking, tolls, accessories,

371
00:14:12,158 --> 00:14:15,436
bed covers, hitches and modifications.

372
00:14:15,616 --> 00:14:18,147
These can add hundreds or thousands of

373
00:14:18,147 --> 00:14:19,146
dollars a year.

374
00:14:19,326 --> 00:14:21,602
They are the ones owners forget to

375
00:14:21,602 --> 00:14:23,879
budget, because they come one at a

376
00:14:23,879 --> 00:14:24,213
time.

377
00:14:24,563 --> 00:14:25,852
So let's add it up.

378
00:14:26,032 --> 00:14:27,916
For a new half-ton pickup,

379
00:14:27,916 --> 00:14:31,612
AAA's twenty twenty-six number is sixteen thousand,

380
00:14:31,612 --> 00:14:34,438
four hundred forty-nine dollars a year.

381
00:14:34,618 --> 00:14:36,615
That is about one thousand,

382
00:14:36,615 --> 00:14:39,425
three hundred seventy dollars a month,

383
00:14:39,425 --> 00:14:42,828
before accessories and before the diesel spike

384
00:14:42,828 --> 00:14:45,194
that came after AAA's fuel data.

385
00:14:45,374 --> 00:14:47,446
That is the real price of truck

386
00:14:47,446 --> 00:14:48,114
ownership.

387
00:14:48,464 --> 00:14:50,415
Now the final twist.

388
00:14:50,595 --> 00:14:52,784
The truck with the lowest sticker price

389
00:14:52,784 --> 00:14:54,693
is not always the cheapest to own.

390
00:14:54,873 --> 00:14:57,182
A truck that holds its value,

391
00:14:57,182 --> 00:14:59,729
is cheap to insure and uses less

392
00:14:59,729 --> 00:15:02,435
fuel can cost less over five years

393
00:15:02,435 --> 00:15:05,380
than a cheaper truck that loses value

394
00:15:05,380 --> 00:15:07,052
fast and drinks fuel.

395
00:15:07,232 --> 00:15:09,693
That is exactly why the hybrid pickup

396
00:15:09,693 --> 00:15:11,888
came out cheapest in AAA's study.

397
00:15:12,237 --> 00:15:14,246
Consider the Ford Maverick.

398
00:15:14,426 --> 00:15:15,715
According to Ford,

399
00:15:15,715 --> 00:15:19,223
the Maverick sold one hundred fifty-five thousand

400
00:15:19,223 --> 00:15:22,230
and fifty-one units in twenty twenty-five,

401
00:15:22,230 --> 00:15:26,024
and eighty-one thousand and thirty-four were hybrids.

402
00:15:26,204 --> 00:15:28,888
Buyers clearly understood that a small hybrid

403
00:15:28,888 --> 00:15:30,976
truck could save money every month.

404
00:15:31,156 --> 00:15:32,913
For twenty twenty-seven,

405
00:15:32,913 --> 00:15:35,989
Ford Authority reports the base Maverick X

406
00:15:35,989 --> 00:15:37,600
L becomes hybrid only.

407
00:15:37,949 --> 00:15:40,281
And the same idea works with bigger

408
00:15:40,281 --> 00:15:40,747
trucks.

409
00:15:40,927 --> 00:15:42,192
According to Ford,

410
00:15:42,192 --> 00:15:44,230
it sold eighty-four thousand,

411
00:15:44,230 --> 00:15:48,025
nine hundred thirty-four F-one-fifty hybrids in twenty

412
00:15:48,025 --> 00:15:50,274
twenty-five, up fifteen percent.

413
00:15:50,454 --> 00:15:53,096
For buyers who need a full-size truck,

414
00:15:53,096 --> 00:15:55,739
the hybrid can trim fuel costs without

415
00:15:55,739 --> 00:15:57,687
giving up towing capability.

416
00:15:58,036 --> 00:16:00,563
Let's put real numbers on a five-year

417
00:16:00,563 --> 00:16:00,904
plan.

418
00:16:01,084 --> 00:16:03,915
Using AAA's half-ton pickup estimate,

419
00:16:03,915 --> 00:16:06,517
five years of ownership adds up to

420
00:16:06,517 --> 00:16:09,118
about eighty-two thousand dollars.

421
00:16:09,298 --> 00:16:11,264
That is more than the price of

422
00:16:11,264 --> 00:16:13,164
the average full-size pickup.

423
00:16:13,344 --> 00:16:14,334
In other words,

424
00:16:14,334 --> 00:16:15,390
over five years,

425
00:16:15,390 --> 00:16:17,436
the cost of keeping a truck can

426
00:16:17,436 --> 00:16:19,613
be bigger than the cost of buying

427
00:16:19,613 --> 00:16:19,811
it.

428
00:16:20,161 --> 00:16:22,945
And that assumes fifteen thousand miles a

429
00:16:22,945 --> 00:16:23,285
year.

430
00:16:23,465 --> 00:16:25,794
Drive twenty thousand miles,

431
00:16:25,794 --> 00:16:28,956
and fuel, tires and maintenance go up.

432
00:16:29,136 --> 00:16:32,520
Drive less, and depreciation becomes a bigger

433
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:33,873
share of the bill,

434
00:16:33,873 --> 00:16:36,805
because the truck loses value even when

435
00:16:36,805 --> 00:16:38,610
it sits in the driveway.

436
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:40,722
There is no way to avoid every

437
00:16:40,722 --> 00:16:42,977
cost, but you can choose which ones

438
00:16:42,977 --> 00:16:43,492
you pay.

439
00:16:43,841 --> 00:16:46,372
Here is the twist many owners miss.

440
00:16:46,552 --> 00:16:48,538
The costs do not stay the same

441
00:16:48,538 --> 00:16:49,199
each year.

442
00:16:49,379 --> 00:16:50,662
In the first years,

443
00:16:50,662 --> 00:16:53,768
depreciation and finance charges are heaviest.

444
00:16:53,948 --> 00:16:55,204
In later years,

445
00:16:55,204 --> 00:16:58,470
depreciation slows and the loan is paid

446
00:16:58,470 --> 00:17:01,401
off, but repairs and tires start to

447
00:17:01,401 --> 00:17:01,820
grow.

448
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,365
Knowing that curve helps you decide when

449
00:17:04,365 --> 00:17:05,962
to keep a truck and when to

450
00:17:05,962 --> 00:17:06,435
sell it.

451
00:17:06,784 --> 00:17:09,281
Many owners find a sweet spot after

452
00:17:09,281 --> 00:17:10,778
the loan is paid off.

453
00:17:10,958 --> 00:17:12,775
If the truck is reliable,

454
00:17:12,775 --> 00:17:15,173
a few years without a payment can

455
00:17:15,173 --> 00:17:16,627
save a lot of money,

456
00:17:16,627 --> 00:17:18,807
even with higher repair bills.

457
00:17:18,987 --> 00:17:22,043
The most expensive habit in truck ownership

458
00:17:22,043 --> 00:17:24,389
is trading in every few years and

459
00:17:24,389 --> 00:17:26,521
starting a new loan each time.

460
00:17:26,871 --> 00:17:28,893
Now let's talk about the people who

461
00:17:28,893 --> 00:17:29,124
tow.

462
00:17:29,304 --> 00:17:32,251
Towing adds costs that AAA's averages do

463
00:17:32,251 --> 00:17:33,356
not fully show.

464
00:17:33,536 --> 00:17:35,466
Towing increases fuel use,

465
00:17:35,466 --> 00:17:38,288
wears brakes and transmissions faster,

466
00:17:38,288 --> 00:17:41,555
and often means following the severe service

467
00:17:41,555 --> 00:17:43,114
maintenance schedule.

468
00:17:43,294 --> 00:17:45,578
A truck that tows every weekend will

469
00:17:45,578 --> 00:17:47,482
cost more to own than the same

470
00:17:47,482 --> 00:17:48,751
truck that does not.

471
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:52,249
And towing can require extra equipment:

472
00:17:52,249 --> 00:17:53,460
a proper hitch,

473
00:17:53,460 --> 00:17:54,994
a brake controller,

474
00:17:54,994 --> 00:17:59,111
wiring, mirrors and sometimes a weight distribution

475
00:17:59,111 --> 00:17:59,596
hitch.

476
00:17:59,776 --> 00:18:02,127
These parts protect your truck and your

477
00:18:02,127 --> 00:18:04,478
safety, so they are worth buying right.

478
00:18:04,658 --> 00:18:06,745
But they belong in your budget before

479
00:18:06,745 --> 00:18:07,874
you buy the trailer.

480
00:18:08,223 --> 00:18:10,464
Work trucks have their own costs.

481
00:18:10,644 --> 00:18:12,493
If you use your truck for a

482
00:18:12,493 --> 00:18:15,505
business, you may need commercial insurance,

483
00:18:15,505 --> 00:18:17,901
which can cost more than a personal

484
00:18:17,901 --> 00:18:19,955
policy, according to Insurify.

485
00:18:20,135 --> 00:18:21,438
On the other hand,

486
00:18:21,438 --> 00:18:24,477
business use can come with tax deductions.

487
00:18:24,657 --> 00:18:26,979
A tax professional can tell you which

488
00:18:26,979 --> 00:18:27,920
applies to you.

489
00:18:28,269 --> 00:18:30,022
Now the electric question.

490
00:18:30,202 --> 00:18:32,949
In AAA's twenty twenty-six numbers,

491
00:18:32,949 --> 00:18:36,246
the electric pickup was the most expensive

492
00:18:36,246 --> 00:18:38,600
to own, at seventeen thousand,

493
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:41,504
four hundred fourteen dollars a year,

494
00:18:41,504 --> 00:18:44,800
even though electricity cost much less per

495
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:45,899
mile than gas.

496
00:18:46,079 --> 00:18:46,323
Why?

497
00:18:46,503 --> 00:18:50,102
Mostly higher purchase prices and depreciation.

498
00:18:50,282 --> 00:18:52,312
Cheaper fuel did not make up for

499
00:18:52,312 --> 00:18:52,883
the rest.

500
00:18:53,232 --> 00:18:55,718
That could change as prices fall and

501
00:18:55,718 --> 00:18:58,550
more used electric trucks hit the market.

502
00:18:58,730 --> 00:18:59,504
But for now,

503
00:18:59,504 --> 00:19:02,084
AAA's study shows that the cheapest fuel

504
00:19:02,084 --> 00:19:05,115
does not automatically mean the cheapest truck.

505
00:19:05,295 --> 00:19:07,779
Fuel is only one of six costs,

506
00:19:07,779 --> 00:19:10,926
and depreciation is still the biggest.

507
00:19:11,276 --> 00:19:13,496
There is also the question of used

508
00:19:13,496 --> 00:19:14,214
versus new.

509
00:19:14,394 --> 00:19:17,600
A used truck usually has lower depreciation

510
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,091
and lower insurance,

511
00:19:19,091 --> 00:19:21,477
but it may need more repairs and

512
00:19:21,477 --> 00:19:23,937
come with a higher interest rate.

513
00:19:24,117 --> 00:19:25,728
According to Experian,

514
00:19:25,728 --> 00:19:28,951
used vehicle loans averaged eleven point one

515
00:19:28,951 --> 00:19:31,661
nine percent in the second quarter of

516
00:19:31,661 --> 00:19:35,176
twenty twenty-six, compared with six point three

517
00:19:35,176 --> 00:19:36,714
five percent for new.

518
00:19:37,063 --> 00:19:39,743
So a used truck is not automatically

519
00:19:39,743 --> 00:19:40,860
cheaper to own.

520
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,319
If you pay cash,

521
00:19:42,319 --> 00:19:44,319
a used truck can be a big

522
00:19:44,319 --> 00:19:44,639
win.

523
00:19:44,819 --> 00:19:46,842
If you finance at a high rate,

524
00:19:46,842 --> 00:19:49,068
the interest can eat the savings.

525
00:19:49,248 --> 00:19:51,627
Compare the total cost of both,

526
00:19:51,627 --> 00:19:54,542
including interest, before you decide.

527
00:19:54,892 --> 00:19:57,569
And one more hidden cost hides inside

528
00:19:57,569 --> 00:19:58,944
the payment itself:

529
00:19:58,944 --> 00:20:01,765
the add-ons sold in the finance office.

530
00:20:01,945 --> 00:20:05,848
Extended warranties, paint protection and service plans

531
00:20:05,848 --> 00:20:07,834
can add thousands to a loan,

532
00:20:07,834 --> 00:20:10,176
and then you pay interest on them

533
00:20:10,176 --> 00:20:10,885
for years.

534
00:20:11,065 --> 00:20:12,251
Some can be useful,

535
00:20:12,251 --> 00:20:14,062
but they are always optional,

536
00:20:14,062 --> 00:20:16,310
and they can usually be bought later

537
00:20:16,310 --> 00:20:17,184
or not at all.

538
00:20:17,533 --> 00:20:19,200
The simple rule is this:

539
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:21,215
if you would not pay cash for

540
00:20:21,215 --> 00:20:22,326
an add-on today,

541
00:20:22,326 --> 00:20:25,174
think twice before financing it for seven

542
00:20:25,174 --> 00:20:25,591
years.

543
00:20:25,771 --> 00:20:28,366
A two thousand dollar product on a

544
00:20:28,366 --> 00:20:30,809
long loan can cost far more once

545
00:20:30,809 --> 00:20:32,412
interest is included.

546
00:20:32,761 --> 00:20:33,888
Before you buy,

547
00:20:33,888 --> 00:20:35,466
run your own numbers.

548
00:20:35,646 --> 00:20:37,588
Look up the insurance quote,

549
00:20:37,588 --> 00:20:40,084
estimate fuel for your real driving,

550
00:20:40,084 --> 00:20:42,303
check the loan's total interest,

551
00:20:42,303 --> 00:20:44,591
and look at resale values for the

552
00:20:44,591 --> 00:20:45,631
truck you want.

553
00:20:45,811 --> 00:20:48,248
Twenty minutes with a calculator can save

554
00:20:48,248 --> 00:20:50,507
you thousands of dollars over the life

555
00:20:50,507 --> 00:20:51,279
of the truck.

556
00:20:51,629 --> 00:20:54,038
So here is your hidden cost checklist

557
00:20:54,038 --> 00:20:55,600
for twenty twenty-seven.

558
00:20:55,780 --> 00:20:59,163
One: estimate depreciation and buy the trims

559
00:20:59,163 --> 00:21:00,470
used buyers want.

560
00:21:00,650 --> 00:21:03,209
Two: compare the total cost of the

561
00:21:03,209 --> 00:21:04,865
loan, not the payment.

562
00:21:05,045 --> 00:21:08,354
Three: get insurance quotes before you choose.

563
00:21:08,534 --> 00:21:11,866
Four: budget for tires and maintenance.

564
00:21:12,046 --> 00:21:14,835
